# CR 612: Magical Hack replaces Plains with Forest in Starfield Shepherd's text while it is a spell on the stack, and the
# permanent it becomes has that text (CR 400.7a). Its enters trigger is put on the stack with the changed text, so its search
# for "a basic Plains card" reads "a basic Forest card": it refuses a basic Plains and takes a basic Forest. (Changed once the
# trigger is already on the stack, the Shepherd's text would not change the trigger's: CR 113.7a.) The warp cost {1}{W} is
# paid with a Plains and Mox Pearl; Magical Hack's {U} with Mox Sapphire.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Starfield Shepherd
Magical Hack
Plains
Forest
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x22

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Starfield Shepherd.Cast(Ability: Warp)
Bot1.Choose(Close mana window)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Magical Hack.Cast(Stack.Starfield Shepherd)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Modes(Plains)
Bot1.Modes(Forest)
! Bot1.Search(Plains)
Bot1.Search(Forest)

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand = Forest
